BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Opera’s Greatest Drama: Love Murder + Heartbreak
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T180000
DTSTAMP:20261018T205153Z
UID:funcheap-1633130@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Live Music Event
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSF Bach ChoirThe San Francisco
  Bach Choir presents Love! Murder! Passion! Grief! Opera!\, an afternoon o
 f soaring arias\, powerful choruses\, larger-than-life characters\, and so
 me of opera’s most unforgettable stories.\nTravel from pioneers in the A
 merican West to the fires of Hell\, from John Brown’s dream of justice t
 o Carmen’s seductive song. Along the way\, audiences will experience mus
 ic filled with love and longing\, drama and deceit\, heartbreak and hope.\
 n\nJoining the San Francisco Bach Choir are four featured soloists: sopran
 o Cara Gabrielson\, alto Sara Couden\, tenor Elliott James Encarnación\, 
 and bass Curtis Streetman. Together\, these mesmerizing vocalists bring op
 era’s heroes\, villains\, lovers\, dreamers\, and larger-than-life perso
 nalities to the stage. Joining our choir members and soloists at the piano
  are Yongyu Gao and Dara Phung.\nHave a drink with Verdi. Weep for Dido. A
 pplaud the Meistersinger. Whether you’re a longtime opera fan or simply 
 curious\, this lively program offers an accessible way to experience the d
 rama\, humor\, beauty\, and emotional power of opera.\n\nAbout the San Fra
 ncisco Bach Choir:\nFounded in 1936\, the San Francisco Bach Choir is one 
 of the Bay Area’s longstanding choral organizations\, bringing together 
 skilled volunteer singers to perform an ambitious repertoire ranging from 
 the music of J.S. Bach and other great choral masters to works spanning ce
 nturies\, cultures\, and musical traditions.\nThe Choir is led by acclaime
 d A...\n\n$15.00\n\nTickets: https://bit.ly/4hPY1wP\nDetails: https://sf.f
 uncheap.com/operas-greatest-drama-love-murder-heartbreak-sf/\nSource: Func
 heap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Octobe
 r-Facebook-Ad-1200x628-1.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261018T205153Z
LOCATION:Calvary Presbyterian Church\, 2515 Fillmore Street (at Jackson) S
 an Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/operas-greatest-drama-love-murder-heartbreak-s
 f/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dinosaur Jr.
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T200000
DTSTAMP:20261019T210249Z
UID:dothebay-17551294@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Another Planet Entertainment presents\nDinosaur Jr.\n\nSunday\
 , October 18 | The Castro\n\nFinally! The sixth studio album Dinosaur Jr. 
 have recorded in the 20 years since their triumphal rebirth. There have be
 en several live and/or closet cleaning collections to keep us punters sate
 d for the five years since Sweep It Into Space\, but there is nothing quit
 e like having a full slab of new Dino tunes to fry your ears. And There Ne
 ar has all knobs set to Extra Crispy.\n\nCreated in short\, intense bursts
  over the course of a year at Amherst’s Bisquiteen Studio\, There Near w
 as recorded almost entirely by Dino’s core trio — king of the thunder 
 tubs\, Murph\, human tornado Lou Barlow on bass/vocals and the inimitable 
 J Mascis on guitar/vocals — with a bit of piano and organ work by local 
 master musician\, Ken Mauri. And the album roars from start to finish.\n\n
 Trying to define the essence of Dino’s sound is never easy. It’s an in
 stantly recognizable blend of loose vocals\, sharp guitars and an animalis
 tic rhythm section\, but these parts combine into a whole far more magical
  and exciting than its components. In strict rock-write terms\, you might 
 call the approach “post-core power balladeering\,” but what use is tha
 t? Dinosaur Jr. invented their formula for noise/pop jiggering around the 
 same time Husker Dü were trying out some of the same ideas\, all of which
  got made popular by a band they inspired called Nirvana. But that’s an 
 old and much-told tale.\n\nJ’s guitar tone throughout There Near is even
  m...\n\nall ages\nSold out\nAnother Planet Entertainment presents\nListed
  time is doors\n\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/18/dinosaur
 -jr-with-special-gueststef-chura-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7619917;-122.4347365
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33051315/6b7d732a-946d-4d6e-9e21-0115ef2e41b8.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261019T210249Z
LOCATION:The Castro\, 429 Castro St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/18/dinosaur-jr-with-special-guests
 tef-chura-tickets
END:VEVENT
