DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerKenzie AelligTricky FM is the 
 music project and “electronica star” alter ego of Hana Freed. Based ou
 t of San Francisco\, she self produces all her own music\, while being a s
 taple in clubs\, venues and punk bars throughout the Bay Area and beyond. 
 On stage\, Tricky FM is known for her energetic and almost performance-art
  interpretation of the ‘pop star’. At home\, behind her computer\, she
 ’s crafted her own brand of euphoric sounding electronica. Her work cent
 ers on the complex terrain of navigating contemporary womanhood: trust\, i
 ntimacy\, fulfillment and ultimately the relationship with the self. Her 2
 023 debut Peace\, Love\, Unity\, Rave (Cherub Dream Records) arrived from 
 a place of urgency and anger—a sampled-based Ableton-coded reckoning wit
 h the ways misogyny runs through every facet of life. This album led her t
 o share stages with Alice Glass\, Molly Nilsson\, Mechatok\, Otha\, Spelll
 ing\, Salami Rose Joe Louis and more.\nHer forthcoming album Twin Star Fan
 tasy finds Tricky FM on the other side of this reckoning. Where PLUR was f
 orged in chaos\, Twin Star Fantasy was built in stillness. What fantastica
 l things can be brought forth from the seemingly everyday and mundane? Thi
 s album weaves reflections on stability and the relationships that shaped 
 her—an homage to the past\, a document of the present\, and a prayer for
  the future. It shows an artist at the fullness of her potential\, steppin
 g into a sound that she has been perfecting on her own. Hana produc...\n\n
 $17.00\n\nTickets: https://www.thelab.org/projects/2026/10/22/cherub-dream
 -records-x-the-lab-tricky-fm-twin-star-fantasy-edgar\nDetails: https://sf.
 funcheap.com/tricky-fms-twin-star-fantasy-record-release-edgar-tugboyz/\nS
 ource: Funcheap SF
