BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Organ Recital: English and American Masterworks
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T190000
DTSTAMP:20261023T114720Z
UID:dothebay-17986121@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Justin Murphy-Mancini from Pacific Lutheran University wil
 l offer a pipe-organ recital on "English and American Masterworks" on the 
 1924 E. M. Skinner organ in the sublime acoustics of Trinity St. Peter's. 
 The program features hidden gems written in the last 150 years. Prominent 
 American composers of yesteryear\, like Henry Dunham\, are contrasted with
  major figures of the 20th century\, including Emma Lou Diemer\, Undine Sm
 ith Moore\, and Miriam Gideon. These are paired with works by composers ac
 ross the pond\, including Kenneth Leighton and Samuel Coleridge-Taylor. Th
 e crown jewel is Herbert Howells's Master Tallis' Testament. This concert 
 has a little of everything\, from Bachian inspired fireworks\, to dense ch
 romaticism\, to unadulterated joy. It is a diverse\, yet coherent musical 
 experience.\n\nFree\n\nPresented by Palo Alto/Peninsula Chapter of the Ame
 rican Guild of Organists\n\nFree\nPalo Alto/Peninsula Chapter of the Ameri
 can Guild of Organists\n\nTickets: http://papenago.org\nDetails: https://d
 othebay.com/events/2026/11/1/organ-recital-english-and-american-masterwork
 s-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/35097363/e3009601-19c3-4394-af08-70e9ac40f78e.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261023T114720Z
LOCATION:Trinity + St. Peter's Episcopal Church\, 1620 Gough Street\, San 
 Francisco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/1/organ-recital-english-and-americ
 an-masterworks-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Musical Box
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17348370@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Renowned for their high quality reproductions of historic Gene
 sis performances since 1993\, The Musical Box takes fans along for a time-
 travel ride\, offering people a chance to relive the magic of this unique 
 experience.\n\nThese replicas has required exhaustive visual\, scenic\, au
 dio and musical research even tracking down the original music instruments
  used at the time. The visual aspect of The Musical Box shows are based on
  thousands of photos and many amateur films taken at the Genesis concerts\
 , as well as the original slides used by the group during their shows.\n\n
 Impressively\, The Musical Box is the only group licensed and supported by
  Genesis and Peter Gabriel and has presented close to 1000 concerts across
  the world to more than one million spectators\, in prestigious amphitheat
 ers such as The Royal Albert Hall in London\, the Olympia in Paris and the
  Bell Center in Montreal.\n\nPeter Gabriel\, who saw the concert was ”re
 ally impressed by the production quality and the attention to detail”\; 
 Steve Hackett and Phil Collins have even joined The Musical Box on stage.\
 n\n''The Musical Box play it better than we did'' stated Phil Collins afte
 r seeing The Musical Box's production in Geneva.\n\nA Musical Box show is 
 a unique opportunity to discover the mystical Genesis concerts and to reli
 ve a historic rock moment.\n\nGoldenvoice Presents\n\nTickets: https://tix
 .axs.com/BTg4EgAAAAA6Joe%2fAgAAAADG%2fv%2f%2f%2fwD%2f%2f%2f%2f%2fC0dvbGRlb
 nZvaWNlAP%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f?cid=usaffdostuff\nDetails: https:/
 /dothebay.com/events/2026/11/1/the-musical-box-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7879104;-122.4215079
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/32075445/7f9fe665-d736-4cd3-9ca5-8656a2774856.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:The Regency Ballroom\, 1290 Sutter Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94109
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/1/the-musical-box-tickets
END:VEVENT
