SUMMARY:GLIDE Holiday Jam 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T193000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17691025@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:GLIDE is thrilled to announce new details for the 2026 GLIDE H
 oliday Jam: Turn It Up and Turn It Out\, headlined by three-time Grammy Aw
 ard winner\, Rock & Roll Hall of Fame inductee\, and recipient of numerous
  lifetime achievement honors Patti LaBelle. Returning to The Warfield in S
 an Francisco on Thursday\, November 5\, the GLIDE Holiday Jam will also fe
 ature powerhouse vocalist Destani Wolf\, traditional Veracruz\, Mexico mus
 ic group Son de Fandango\, and the legendary GLIDE Ensemble and The Change
  Band\, led by Zoe Ellis.\n\nFor more than 40 years\, the GLIDE Holiday Ja
 m has brought together acclaimed artists\, community leaders\, and support
 ers for an unforgettable evening of music\, inspiration\, and hope while r
 aising critical funds for GLIDE's mission of unconditional love\, radical 
 inclusion\, and social justice. A beloved Bay Area tradition\, the GLIDE H
 oliday Jam is where legendary artists meet everyday heroes\, the spirit of
  the season shines brightest\, and the community comes together to support
  GLIDE's life-changing programs\, including meals\, housing\, recovery\, h
 ealth access\, and services for women and families.\n\nPatti LaBelle has c
 aptivated audiences for more than six decades with her extraordinary voice
 \, electrifying stage presence\, and enduring catalog of hits. Known world
 wide as the "Godmother of Soul\," she has sold more than 50 million record
 s and remains one of the most celebrated and influential performers in Ame
 rican music.\n\n"It has long been a dream to welcome Patti LaBell...\n\nOr
 chestra seating with plated dinner: $550 + fees\; Balcony seating: $125 + 
 fees\nListed time is doors\n\nTickets: https://www.glide.org/holidayjam/\n
 Details: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/5/glide-holiday-jam-2026-tick
 ets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7827039;-122.4103578
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34363539/f6bbc7de-8087-460f-9ca6-b59cbb4dac73.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:The Warfield\, 982 Market St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/5/glide-holiday-jam-2026-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Black Angels
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T210000
DTSTAMP:20261008T185326Z
UID:dothebay-17227487@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Goldenvoice Presents\nPassover Tour 2026\nThe Black Angels\nTh
 ursday\, November 5 | ​The Regency Ballroom\n\n2026 marks the 20th anniv
 ersary of the band’s debut album\, Passover (2006)\, a now-classic recor
 d that helped define the 21st-century psych revival. To celebrate\, The Bl
 ack Angels - Alex Maas (vocals/bass)\, Christian Bland (guitar)\, Stephani
 e Bailey (drums)\, Jake Garcia (guitar)\, and Misti Hamrick (bass) are ret
 urning to the road to perform the album in full\, along with their greates
 t hits.\n\nFormed in Austin\, Texas in 2004\, The Black Angels have become
  one of the most influential bands of the modern psychedelic rock movement
 . Drawing inspiration from forebears such as Syd Barrett\, Roky Erickson\,
  Arthur Lee\, and The Velvet Underground\, the band crafts a sound that is
  both reverent to the genre’s roots and fiercely forward-looking\, hypno
 tic\, heavy\, political\, and immersive.\n\nBeyond their own recordings\, 
 the band’s impact on the global psychedelic community is cemented by the
 ir role as founders of Austin Psych Fest\, one of the world’s most impor
 tant gatherings for psychedelic\, experimental\, and underground music.\n\
 nFollowing albums such as Death Song (2017) and Wilderness of Mirrors (202
 2) on Partisan Records\, The Black Angels continue to evolve while remaini
 ng unmistakably themselves: a band that channels the spirit of classic psy
 chedelia into a dark\, modern\, and deeply powerful form.\n\nIf tickets in
  the accessible section are unavailable\, please reach out to the venue fo
 r accomm...\n\nAll Ages\nGoldenvoice Presents: Passover Tour 2026\nListed 
 time is doors\n\nTickets: https://www.theregencyballroom.com/events/detail
 /?event_id=1408471\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/5/the-bla
 ck-angels-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay\n\nAlso listed on:\n- https://sf.funch
 eap.com/black-angels/
GEO:37.7879104;-122.4215079
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/31514384/951aacba-e5ce-4ed9-8e90-d6b6fbc99d21.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T185326Z
LOCATION:The Regency Ballroom\, 1290 Sutter Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94109
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/5/the-black-angels-tickets
END:VEVENT
