CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Another Planet Entertainment Presents\nThe 30th Arab Film Fest
 ival\nEdward Said: Between Worlds\nSunday\, November 8 | The Castro\n\nThe
  flagship event of the Arab Film and Media Institute\, the Arab Film Festi
 val is the longest running independent festival of its kind in North Ameri
 ca. This year we are celebrating our 30th anniversary!\n\nLaunched in 1996
 \, the festival’s mission is to present the best of contemporary films t
 hat illuminate the richness of Arab culture through authentic narratives a
 nd images\, providing insight into the beauty and complexity of the Arab w
 orld.\n\nThe festival also offers special programming to local audiences\,
  and unprecedented access to the diversity and range of authentic Arab exp
 eriences. The festival has gained an international reputation for excellen
 ce and offers its audiences access to media that reflects the lives of und
 er-represented and provocative themes and groups on a cultural and societa
 l level.\n\nThe 30th edition of the Arab Film Festival will open on Thursd
 ay Nov. 5th at the AMC Kabuki 8 in San Francisco. The festival will run th
 rough Saturday Nov. 14th.\n\nall ages\nAnother Planet Entertainment Presen
 ts: The 30th Arab Film Festival\nListed time is doors\n\nTickets: https://
 thecastro.com/events/edward-said-between-worlds\nDetails: https://dothebay
 .com/events/2026/11/8/edward-said-between-worlds-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
