DESCRIPTION:Sun\, Nov 22\, 3:15pm Concert\; 4:00pm Evensong\n\nJoin us at 
 St. Luke's Episcopal Church in San Francisco\nSt. Luke's Episcopal Church 
 warmly invites you to an afternoon of inspiring music and reflection at 17
 55 Clay Street (@ Van Ness)\, San Francisco\, CA 94109.\nFor directions or
  more information\, visit www.stlukessf.org\nor contact us at (415) 673-73
 27 * office@stlukessf.org\n\nComplimentary parking is available at the Old
  First Garage (1725 Sacramento St.)\n\n3:15pm- Organ Concert-Eric Choate\n
 Eric Choate is a composer\, conductor\, and organist whose music has been 
 praised for its "highly inventive approach to the interleaving of polyphon
 ic voices" (The Rehearsal Studio) and described as "rapturous" and "quietl
 y majestic" (Textura.org). His works are published by E.C. Schirmer and VO
 CES8 Publishing\, with recordings on the Priory Records\, Arsis Audio and 
 Ulysses Arts labels. His music has been performed by artists including VOC
 ES8\, musicians of the San Francisco Symphony\, Berkeley Symphony\, Americ
 an Bach Soloists\, Las Cruces Symphony\, Friction Quartet\, Brian Thorsett
 \, and choirs worldwide.\n\n4:00pm- Evensong with St. Luke's Choir\n\nFree
 \n\nPresented by St. Luke's Episcopal Church.\n\nFree\nSt. Luke's Episcopa
 l Church\n\nTickets: https://www.stlukessf.org/welcome\nDetails: https://d
 othebay.com/events/2026/11/22/concert-evensong-at-st-luke-s-episcopal-chur
 ch-eric-choate-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
