SUMMARY:Venna
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261218T210000
DTSTAMP:20261019T210249Z
UID:dothebay-17714156@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Another Planet Entertainment presents\nVenna\n\nFriday\, Decem
 ber 8 | The Castro\n\nAfter two EPs and an illuminating start to his caree
 r\, Grammy Award-winning saxophonist Venna releases his debut album\, MALI
 K.\n\nFor Venna\, it’s been a whirlwind of a journey to arrive at this p
 oint. He’s spent the better part of three years on the road touring\, wh
 ile coming back to London intermittently. In the spaces he finds himself i
 n as a musician\, he’s often the youngest in the room. This period gave 
 him the confidence to embark on this next stage of his career.\n\n“Every
  experience\, every memory\, every conversation\, anything new\, any encou
 nter has influenced how this album sounds. I might like a particular guita
 r tone from it\, and then I bring it into my world. Everything has come an
 d conjured into one place\, and it’s beautiful to also hear and see\,”
  Venna says.\n\nSpeaking on how he found the words to sing: “Does anyone
  really have the words to say? I don’t know. I don’t know if I had the
  words to say. I just conjured words and thoughts and tried to make art ou
 t of it.”\n\nFeaturing vocals from Jorja Smith\, Cari\, Leon Thomas\, Sm
 ino\, MIKE\, and himself\, MALIK is where listeners can get lost and find 
 themselves again. The album also features a long list of musicians includi
 ng Rocco Palladino\, Elijah Fox\, AoD\, J Warner\, Marco Bernardis and lon
 gtime collaborator\, Yussef Dayes.\n\nMALIK embodies the melting pot of so
 unds that reflects Venna’s environment. Venna doesn’t want to be roote
 d in jazz alone\; his...\n\nall ages\nAnother Planet Entertainment present
 s\nListed time is doors\n\nTickets: https://thecastro.com/events/venna-261
 218\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/18/venna-tickets\nSource
 : DoTheBay
GEO:37.7619917;-122.4347365
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33811451/900f22aa-fc40-4850-b1de-e92144fb9b35.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261019T210249Z
LOCATION:The Castro\, 429 Castro St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94114
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/12/18/venna-tickets
